out.push(A('⚠ **One student declares their limit and the room offers the convenience three times, each time more reasonably, while counting the words of each restatement.** **Any increase is a position.** **In this class the third version has grown in seven of ten cases, always by a clause of justification.** **Then Mrs Oueidat\'s word, and do not let the room hear it as a story about a dishonest colleague: nobody in a corridor thinks they are asking for a misrendering.**'));

// ===================== 14.6 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('14.6  The report in which nobody is the villain'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **The reader and the action, and the second is the one that matters.** **Eight of ten reports go to somebody who was not at the meeting and who will decide something.** **Two go to a file**, which is a different genre: a file report may record a verdict because nobody will act on it for years — **and 14.6b names that, so do not let the two students with file reports write to the eight\'s rules.**'));
out.push(A('**b** Belong: **2** and **4**. ⚠ **2 attributes the correction to the party who made it; 4 gives both reasons and points at where they are.** **1, 3 and 5 all carry a winner** — _eventually accepted_, _despite some initial resistance_, _our position was the stronger_ — **and the room should name the word in each: _eventually_, _despite_, _stronger_.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — ⚠ **make either party the one who gave way**, because the reader acts on the report and a party recorded as having given way will not give way again.'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** ⚠ **_Eventually_, _despite_ and _accepted_.** **_Eventually_ says somebody held out, _despite_ says somebody resisted, and _accepted_ says somebody was right and somebody came round.**   **2** ⚠ **_The directorate conceded the arithmetic_** — **and the directorate did not concede anything: it read the annexe and the annexe was right, which is not a concession, it is reading.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The audience nobody writes for is the party the report describes, and this is the finding of the cycle.** **A report is written for the reader who decides and read by the party it is about** — **their office reads it before the next meeting, which is the only audience that will ever act on the word _eventually_.** **Say that before Stage 3 and the three words will go out of every draft in the room.** ⚠ **And the verb arrives by itself, which is why the remedy is mechanical.** **Nobody chooses _conceded_**: it is the ordinary word for what happened and it carries a winner inside it. **The only defence is to stop at every verb and say it aloud** — **_accepted_, _conceded_, _agreed to_, _came round_, _was persuaded_** — **and a report containing any of the five has a villain in it whether the writer intended one or not.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('**1** _Eventually accepted_ → _both parties accept the return; no figure is agreed._   **2** _Despite resistance_ → _both parties came with a reason, and the reasons are at 3._   **3** ⚠ _Conceded the arithmetic_ → _read the annexe and agrees the figures; it had not previously had them in that form._   **4** **A correction the other party made** → _the office\'s figure was arrived at before the tolerance was excluded, and the office said so._   **5** **A disagreement not resolved** → ⚠ _the regulation does not define the word; the parties disagree, and it is recorded so that neither has to discover it again._'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card A)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Row 1** _Both parties accept the return for the twelve months to March. No figure is agreed and none needs to be._',
  '**Row 2** ⚠ **Already clean.** **Two reasons and a pointer.** **Change nothing.**',
  '**Row 3** _The directorate read the annexe and agrees the figures. It had not previously had them in that form._',
  '**Row 4** ⚠ **Already clean.** **The correction is attributed to the party who made it.** **Change nothing.**',
  '**Row 5** ⚠ **The worst on the card and the repair is a different sentence, not a gentler verb.** _Both parties set out the basis of their figure; the basis of each is at 2 and 3._',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card B)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Row 1** _Both parties came with a reason for the date, and the reasons are set out at 3._',
  '**Row 2** ⚠ **Already clean.** **An undefined word and a recorded disagreement.**',
  '**Row 3** _The inspector read the photographed pages and agrees the count._',
  '**Row 4** ⚠ **Already clean.** **A practice named, and nobody\'s judgement.**',
  '**Row 5** ⚠ **The worst on the card.** _The branch states that three queries were dealt with at the counter; the inspectorate notes that nothing requires them to be entered._ **No obligation, no concession, two facts.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3R · Perform – listener task'));
out.push(A('**Rows 2 and 4 on both cards are already clean and B changes nothing**, which half the room will not believe. ⚠ **Rows 5 are the worst on either card and the room will try to soften the verb**: _was obliged to concede_ becomes _conceded_ becomes _accepted_, and all three have a winner. **The repair is a different sentence**, which says what each party put on the table — **and the listener should say which of the two versions is shorter, because the clean one always is.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 4 · Your turn (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**My first paragraph, before the verb pass.** _The desk eventually accepted that a note attached to copy is read, despite some initial reluctance, and agreed to attach them from March._',
  '⚠ **Three verbs struck: _accepted_, _agreed to_, and the adverb _eventually_, with _despite_ for good measure.**',
  '**After.** _Both parties set out how notes are handled: the desk handles them in a batch at midnight, and the branch files them with the copy. From March notes travel with the copy._',
  '**b** ⚠ **My partner could not tell which party gave way and could say what each one wanted** — **which is the pair of answers the cycle is for.**',
  '**And the figure.** **My first paragraph lost four verbs and eleven words**, and it says more than it did.',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 4R · Report (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE(['Mrs Khoury said the first thing to strike in the report of a negotiation is three words that are in almost every first draft: eventually, despite and accepted. Mr Attar said those are neutral words, and none of the three is neutral: eventually says somebody held out, despite says somebody resisted, and accepted says somebody was right and somebody came round, and a reader who was not in the room learns from them which party gave way. Mrs Oueidat asked why that matters to the reader, and it does not matter to the reader at all, which is the point: it matters to the next meeting, because a party recorded as having given way will not give way again, and the report is read by their office before the next negotiation. Mr Tayara said his first draft had all three, and something worse: he had written that the directorate conceded the arithmetic, and the directorate did not concede anything, they read the annexe and it was right, which is not a concession but reading. Dr Qabbani asked what goes in instead, and Mrs Oueidat said what each party had and where it is: both parties came with a reason for the date they wanted, and the reasons are set out at 3, with no verb of surrender anywhere. Mrs Tarabishi said that sounds evasive, and it is the opposite, because an evasive report leaves out what happened and this one records everything and no opinion about who deserved it. Mrs Rizk asked about a correction, since theirs was wrong about the four pallets, and record that they corrected it and record that they corrected it: the second clause costs nothing and buys the next meeting. Mrs Ajouz asked about where nobody corrected anything, and then the disagreement is recorded as a disagreement, with both positions, the absence of a definition and no resolution. Mr Zahreddine asked whether there is ever a villain, and there is sometimes a system and never a party: the five reports in this class that named a system were acted on and the three that named a party produced replies about the naming. And Mr Tayara said the thing he will take away is the word conceded: he used it about a directorate that had simply read his annexe, and if the report had gone as drafted somebody in that office would have read it before their next meeting. Mrs Khoury said that is the audience nobody writes for, because a report is written for the reader who decides and read by the party it describes. And Mrs Oueidat said the thing she will take away is that the verb arrives by itself: nobody chooses conceded, and the only defence is to stop at every verb and say it out loud.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **The last line is the one to carry out of the cycle: he used _conceded_ about a directorate that had simply read his annexe, and somebody in that office would have read it before their next meeting.** **Mr Tayara caught it himself in a draft.** **Say that**: the only reason the sentence did not go out is that he stopped at every verb, **which is a mechanical check and not a judgement about his own fairness.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ _Eventually_ → **somebody held out.**   **2** _Despite_ → **somebody resisted.**   **3** ⚠ _Accepted_ / _conceded_ / _came round_ / _was persuaded_ / _agreed to_ → **five verbs, each with a winner inside it.**   **4** **_Read_ written as _conceded_** → **the commonest single error in the genre.**   **5** ⚠ **A correction recorded without its author** → **a correction turned into a defeat.**   **6** **A party named where a system would do** → **three such reports in this class produced replies about the naming.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **It gives both parties\' reasons and calls both of them good.** _Neither reason was known to the other party before the meeting and both are good._ **Fourteen words** — **and a report without that sentence reads as neutral prose hiding a verdict, because that is what most reports are.**'));
out.push(A('**2** ⚠ **Whether a double session counts as one session for the purposes of the cycle, and that the regulation does not define _session_.** **It is recorded so that the next meeting does not rediscover it** — **and an unrecorded disagreement is rediscovered by both parties at full length.**'));
out.push(A('**3** ⚠ **An earlier draft said the directorate conceded the arithmetic; it did not, it read the annexe, which it had not previously been sent in that form.** **He says the difference between those two sentences is what the next meeting will start from** — **which is the plainest statement of the cycle\'s finding anybody in this class has written.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 6 · Write with help (sample)'));
