out.push(A('**b** ⚠ **That the minute is wrong.** **It is not.** **_Proposed by neither party before the meeting_ is accurate** — **and what is wrong with it is that it denies the credit to everybody, including the party that earned it, which is a different fault and needs a different remedy.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the second mediation of Book 2 and the fourteenth of the level, and what is new is that the record is accurate and still wrong.** **In 13.7 the minute contained a judgement that could be answered.** **Here every word is true.** **The fault is an omission produced by the writer\'s own care** — **and that is a shape the room has not met: a sentence that is accurate, modest, and denies something to somebody who earned it.** ⚠ **Declining credit is not giving it.** **Credit is a positive act in a record.** **A writer who only declines to take it has left the record saying that nothing happened** — **and _by neither party before the meeting_ is the exact form of that mistake, because it is true of both parties and informative about neither.**'));
