out.push(SAMPLE(['Mrs Khoury said nobody gets the letter: the minute gets an amendment and it is one clause. Mrs Rizk asked whether not a letter to the officer, and a letter would explain a sentence to the person complaining about it, and the sentence is in a document his director reads, so a complaint about a record is answered by the record. Mrs Oueidat said so the clause goes, and Mrs Rizk gave the amendment: proposed by neither party before the meeting becomes proposed by the regional office in the meeting, eight words for eight words, and his director reads the second one. Dr Qabbani asked why the first version was written at all, and because she was trying not to claim it: she knew it was not hers and wrote a clause that said so, and by neither party before the meeting is accurate and denies the credit to everybody including the party that earned it. Mrs Khoury said a report that avoids claiming credit has not thereby given it to anybody, because credit is a positive act in a record, and a writer who only declines to take it leaves the record saying that nothing happened. Mr Tayara said the branch\'s own account is incomplete too, and Mrs Oueidat said it leaves out that requesting the documents delayed the figure by three days, and neither party is being unfair: each has written down what they did. Mrs Tarabishi said so both accounts need the other, and both are what each party can see, and the useful move is not to reconcile them but to find the one sentence in the record that is wrong because of what neither party could see. Mrs Ajouz asked about the delay, and it goes in because it is hers. Mr Zahreddine asked whether the officer comes out of it well, and he comes out as the party who proposed the principle and said so when the record did not. Mr Attar asked whether an amendment is not an admission, and an amendment within a fortnight is a correction and after six months it is an admission. And Mrs Rizk said the thing she will take away is that she was being careful: she wrote the clause to avoid taking credit she had not earned, and the careful version denied it to the man who had. Mrs Oueidat said that is the finding of the unit and not of the cycle, because every move in these seven has been a way of giving the other party something true. And Mr Tayara said the thing he will take away is the eighth of February, because an amendment in three days cost nothing and the same amendment in June would have been an admission.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **Two lines to carry out of the unit.** **Mrs Rizk\'s: she wrote the clause to avoid taking credit she had not earned, and the careful version denied it to the man who had.** **And Mr Tayara\'s eighth of February: an amendment in three days cost nothing and the same amendment in June would have been an admission.** **Say both.** **The first is the finding and the second is the only reason the finding could be acted on.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **A letter to the officer** → **it explains a sentence to the person complaining about it, and the sentence stays where his director reads it.**   **2** _The minute is inaccurate_ → **it is accurate; that is the whole difficulty.**   **3** ⚠ **Credit declined rather than given** → **the record then says nothing happened.**   **4** **The writer\'s own delay left out** → **a record carrying only the writer\'s good decisions will be annotated by the other party.**   **5** ⚠ **An amendment deferred to the next meeting** → **three days is a correction and six months is an admission.**   **6** **A letter written on Pair B** → **the record carries both accounts.**'));
